# ---- Firebase (Firestore + Auth) ---------------------------------------------
# 1. console.firebase.google.com → create a project (e.g. "noteflow").
# 2. Build → Authentication → Get started → Sign-in method → enable
#    "Email/Password".
# 3. Project settings → Your apps → Add web app → copy the apiKey →
#    FIREBASE_API_KEY.
# 4. Project settings → Service accounts → Generate new private key → download
#    the JSON, then set:
#      FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID    = project_id    from that JSON
#      FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL  = client_email  from that JSON
#      FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY   = private_key   from that JSON
#    Keep the \n sequences in the private key as literal "\n" (the app converts
#    them). In Vercel, also paste it with literal \n, not actual newlines.
# 5. Firestore Database → Create database → Production mode → a region close to
#    your users. Publish firebase/firestore.rules to block direct client access.

FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=""
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=""
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=""
FIREBASE_API_KEY=""